Foresight v1.0: the demonstration, on the morning of 2026-01-01
in a temporary installation with the sandbox's models

1  The monthly list                                       make score
   cohort marked 2025-12-31: 283 contracts, 40 calls, 20 held out at
   random; 2 key accounts listed apart
    1  Hartton Cleaning      76.5%  Last order 274 days ago
    2  Hartdale Nursery      44.5%  Last order 118 days ago
    3  Greyworth Dental      43.4%  Last order 165 days ago
   the next night: done already, list made by run 1

2  Next quarter's demand                    make score ARGS=forecast
   from 2025-12: 720 product-region months written, each with an 80%
   range

3  The API                                                make serve
   GET /health: ok; renewal v1, triage v1; Platt's map as fitted
   POST /renewal 15378: list, 76.5%; on the list, held out this
   month: no call; run 1
   POST /renewal "15378": 422, input should be a valid integer
   POST /triage: Urgent, Delivery (model (unsure))
   GET /forecast/MRD-CLE-001/Midwest: 2026-01, 563 units (428 to
   652)

4  The monitor                                       the weekly page
   chances: average 8.8%, PSI 0.05 against the 10,778 rows the model
   learned from
   inputs over a PSI of 0.25, and how far they move the average log-
   odds:
     tenure_days       0.91   +0.007
     discount_pct      0.33   -0.036
     legacy_terms      0.32   -0.022
   order feed: cost alert 2025-01-01, Voss Industrial
   order feed: price alert 2025-02-01, Voss Industrial
   this list's notices are due 2026-01-30, its outcomes on
   2026-04-01

5  The MCP server                     python -m foresight.mcp_server
   tools/list: renewal_risk, why, demand_forecast
   renewal_risk(region="Midwest"): 8 of the 40 calls, 4 of them held
   out; first, Warebury Nursery (30.8%), last order 132 days ago
   (typical: 13)

6  It fails correctly
   the job on 2026-01-30: refused, orders on record to 2025-12-31;
   the list marked 2026-01-30 needs them to 2026-01-29
   POST /renewal 16000: 409, contract 16000 is not at its mark until
   2026-03-02
   no model in the registry: answered by the rule, "Last order 274
   days ago"
   renewal_risk(region="Mid-west"): refused by the schema: Input
   should be 'Midwest', 'Northeast', 'Southeast', 'Southwest' or
   'West'

7  The evidence
   run: renewal  2025-12-31  finished at done
   run: forecast 2025-12-01  finished at done
   run: renewal  2026-01-30  failed   at fresh
   holdout.csv: 40 contracts, 20 held out, drawn once
   the 283 rows the list scored, scored again: largest change
   0.0e+00
   renewal v1's model card, beside it in the registry: 122 lines
